# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Windows checkouts convert LF -> CRLF by default, which makes `gofmt -l` report every .go
# file as unformatted (CRLF is not gofmt's output) and fails the `make check` fmt gate on the
# windows/amd64 CI row. Pinning eol=lf keeps one canonical form everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored native libs and the C header they ship with: never touched by eol conversion.
*.a binary
*.zip binary
